---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";

const contact = "privacy@openimages.cloud";
const updated = "2026-11-14";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy and legal notice"
  description="What Open Image Cloud collects when you visit the website or download an image, who processes it, and who publishes the project."
>
  <article class="text-ink-muted mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 leading-relaxed sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="text-ink mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy and legal notice</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      Short version: no account, no cookie, no tracker, no advertising. The website and the image
      downloads only handle the technical data any web server sees, and download counts are kept
      without IP addresses.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Who is responsible</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Open Image Cloud is a non-profit community project published by Kevin Allioli, who is the
        controller for the processing described here. Contact:{" "}
        <a class="link" href={`mailto:${contact}`}>
          {contact}
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The website</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>
          openimages.cloud is a static site served by Cloudflare. To deliver a page, Cloudflare
          necessarily receives your IP address, browser user agent and the requested address, and
          keeps short-lived technical logs to operate and protect the service.
        </li>
        <li>
          There is no analytics tool, no cookie and no third-party script, font or embed. Fonts are
          served from the site itself.
        </li>
        <li>
          The light or dark theme you pick is stored in your browser (local storage) and never sent
          to us.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Image downloads</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>
          Images are downloaded from images.openimages.cloud, which runs on Cloudflare and fetches
          the files from object storage at Infomaniak in Switzerland. Infomaniak only sees
          Cloudflare, not your address.
        </li>
        <li>
          To publish download statistics, each download records the image, version and file, the
          country derived by Cloudflare, the first word of the client's user agent (for example
          "curl" or "mozilla") and the response size. No IP address and no identifier is stored.
          These records are kept for 90 days at most; only daily totals may be kept longer.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Email and GitHub</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        If you write to an openimages.cloud address, your message is used only to answer it. Issues,
        pull requests and discussions happen on GitHub, under GitHub's own privacy policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Purpose and legal basis</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The data above is processed only to run the website and the downloads, keep them secure and
        publish aggregate download counts. This relies on a legitimate interest in operating the
        service. Nothing is sold, shared for advertising or used to build profiles.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Under the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection and, where it applies, the GDPR, you can ask
        for access to, correction or deletion of data about you, and object to its processing, by
        writing to{" "}
        <a class="link" href={`mailto:${contact}`}>
          {contact}
        </a>
        . You can also complain to the Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner or
        to the data protection authority of your country.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Legal notice</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Publisher: Kevin Allioli. Contact:{" "}
        <a class="link" href={`mailto:${contact}`}>
          {contact}
        </a>
        . Hosting: Cloudflare, Inc. (website and download front end) and Infomaniak Network SA,
        Geneva, Switzerland (image storage). Distribution names and logos are trademarks of their
        respective owners; Open Image Cloud is not affiliated with them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-ink-faint mt-12 text-sm">Last updated {updated}.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
